description:
## Background

crates/cli/src/lib.rs has three dispatch functions called from perform_compilation():
- compile_bundle() (lines ~307–358, ~52 lines)
- compile_merged() (lines ~363–418, ~56 lines)
- compile_per_file() (lines ~423–462, ~40 lines)

compile_bundle and compile_merged are nearly identical — both create a RheoWorld, call generate_bundle_entry(), inject it, build a PluginContext, and call plugin.compile(). The only difference is the output path:
- compile_bundle: uses plugin_output_dir directly (directory for multi-file output)
- compile_merged: uses plugin_output_dir/project_name.ext (single file)

compile_per_file is dead code — no active plugin has uses_bundle_api()=false AND default_merge()=false simultaneously.

compile_one_file() (lines ~255–302) is only used by compile_per_file(), so it also goes.

## File to modify

crates/cli/src/lib.rs

## Task

1. Delete compile_per_file() (~40 lines).

2. Delete compile_one_file() and PerFileCtx (~60 lines).

3. Merge compile_bundle() and compile_merged() into a single compile_with_bundle():

```rust
fn compile_with_bundle(
    plugin: &dyn FormatPlugin,
    output: &Path,          // caller provides the resolved output path
    project: &ProjectConfig,
    output_config: &OutputConfig,
    spine: &TracedSpine,
    plugin_section: &PluginSection,
    resolved_inputs: HashMap<&'static str, PathBuf>,
    results: &mut CompilationResults,
    compilation_root: &Path,
) -> Result<()> {
    let plugin_library = plugin.typst_library().map(|s| s.to_string());
    let mut bundle_world = RheoWorld::new(
        compilation_root,
        spine.documents.first().map(|d| d.path.as_path()).unwrap_or(compilation_root),
        plugin_library,
    )?;
    let bundle_entry_source = generate_bundle_entry(
        spine, compilation_root, plugin.name(), plugin.typst_library().unwrap_or_default(),
    );
    bundle_world.inject_bundle_entry(bundle_entry_source);
    let options = RheoCompileOptions::new(output, &project.root, &mut bundle_world);
    let ctx = PluginContext { project, output_config, options, spine: spine.clone(),
        config: plugin_section.clone(), inputs: resolved_inputs };
    match plugin.compile(ctx) {
        Ok(_) => results.record_success(plugin.name()),
        Err(e) => { error\!(error = %e, "{} compilation failed", plugin.name()); results.record_failure(plugin.name()); }
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

4. In perform_compilation(), replace the three-way dispatch with:

```rust
let output = if spine.merge {
    plugin_output_dir.join(&project.name).with_extension(plugin.output_extension())
} else {
    plugin_output_dir.clone()
};
compile_with_bundle(plugin.as_ref(), &output, project, output_config, &spine,
    &plugin_section, resolved_inputs, &mut results, &compilation_root)?;
```

## Expected outcome

- cargo test passes
- cargo clippy -- -D warnings passes
- ~180 lines removed from cli/src/lib.rs
- All three formats (HTML, PDF, EPUB) compile correctly
- Merged and non-merged PDF modes both work

Background: crates/tests/tests/harness.rs already has test_asset_path_override (line 873) and test_asset_path_override_subdirectory (line 945) demonstrating end-to-end override of css_stylesheet/js_scripts via a single [html.assets] block. This issue adds the equivalent end-to-end test for the new [[html.assets]] multi-block syntax with the default copy-each combiner.

Steps:

1. In crates/tests/tests/harness.rs, add the test below near the existing asset-path-override tests (around line 873), using the same std::process::Command pattern as test_asset_path_override:

   #[test]
   fn test_asset_multiple_blocks_default_combiner() {
       let dir = tempfile::tempdir().expect("Failed to create temp dir");
       let project_path = dir.path();

       std::fs::write(project_path.join("one.css"), "/* one */").unwrap();
       std::fs::write(project_path.join("two.css"), "/* two */").unwrap();
       std::fs::write(project_path.join("one.js"),  "// one").unwrap();
       std::fs::write(project_path.join("two.js"),  "// two").unwrap();
       std::fs::write(project_path.join("hello.typ"), "Hello").unwrap();

       let toml = format!(
           "version = \"{}\"\n\
            formats = [\"html\"]\n\
            [[html.assets]]\n\
            css_stylesheet = \"one.css\"\n\
            js_scripts     = \"one.js\"\n\
            [[html.assets]]\n\
            css_stylesheet = \"two.css\"\n\
            js_scripts     = \"two.js\"\n",
           env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")
       );
       std::fs::write(project_path.join("rheo.toml"), toml).unwrap();

       let build_dir = project_path.join("build");
       let output = std::process::Command::new("cargo")
           .args([
               "run", "-p", "rheo", "--",
               "compile", project_path.to_str().unwrap(),
               "--html",
               "--build-dir", build_dir.to_str().unwrap(),
           ])
           .env("TYPST_IGNORE_SYSTEM_FONTS", "1")
           .output()
           .expect("Failed to run rheo compile");

       assert!(
           output.status.success(),
           "Compilation failed: {}",
           String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stderr)
       );

       for f in ["one.css", "two.css", "one.js", "two.js"] {
           assert!(build_dir.join("html").join(f).exists(), "missing {}", f);
       }

       let html = std::fs::read_to_string(build_dir.join("html/hello.html")).unwrap();
       assert!(html.contains("one.css") && html.contains("two.css"),
               "html should link both stylesheets:\n{}", html);
       assert!(html.contains("one.js") && html.contains("two.js"),
               "html should reference both scripts:\n{}", html);
   }

Acceptance:
- cargo test -p rheo-tests test_asset_multiple_blocks_default_combiner passes
- All four files appear in build/html/
- Generated HTML links both stylesheets and references both scripts

