- Use `html_utils::inject_head_links` (the free function), not `HtmlDom::parse / inject / serialize` directly. The serialize method is named `serialize()` — do not write `to_string()`.
- Use the `STYLESHEETS` and `SCRIPTS` constants, matching the existing `compile()` method at lines 124-125.
- Bind `built_relative_path` as `&str` via `as_str()` from the start, matching lines 132-135 and 144-146 of `compile()`. Do not collect to `Vec<String>` and then re-borrow.
- Early-return when there is nothing to inject (avoids a needless read/write cycle).
- This pass injects head links only; inline styles are already injected by `compile()` if needed (see lines 148-153) and post-compile auto-detected packages never contribute inline styles.

