Problem: On systems without a user cache directory (some CI containers, NixOS, etc.), `dirs::cache_dir()` returns `None` and the fallback silently uses `"."` (current working directory). This means `@preview/` package resolution looks for packages at `./typst/packages/<name>/<version>`, which will almost certainly fail, but the error message will say something like:

