    plugin.as_ref(), plugin_section, project, &typst_cache_dir,
)?;
```

The rest of Phase 1 (resolve_assets, copy_glob_patterns × 3) is unchanged.

2. Track output paths written during compilation. Introduce a small local `Vec<PathBuf>`:

```rust
let mut written_outputs: Vec<PathBuf> = Vec::new();
```

In the `if spine.merge` branch (around line 738), after `plugin.compile(ctx)` succeeds, push `output_path.clone()` to `written_outputs`.

In the `else` (per-file) branch, modify `compile_one_file` (`crates/cli/src/lib.rs:341-370`) — or its caller — to return the output path it wrote, and push it onto `written_outputs` on success. The simplest change: have `compile_one_file` return `Result<PathBuf>` (the path it wrote) and have each caller push the result.

3. After the merged-vs-per-file compile block ends (~line 800), add Phase 2 — extracted into a helper for readability:

```rust
fn run_post_compilation_phase(
    plugin: &dyn FormatPlugin,
    plugin_section: &PluginSection,
    project: &ProjectConfig,
    plugin_output_dir: &Path,
    written_outputs: &[PathBuf],
) -> Result<()> {
    if !plugin_section.auto_detect_packages_enabled() {
        return Ok(());
    }
    let auto_blocks = build_auto_detected_package_blocks(plugin, project);
    if auto_blocks.is_empty() {
        return Ok(());
    }
    let auto_assets = resolve_assets(
        plugin, plugin_section, &auto_blocks, &project.root, plugin_output_dir,
    )?;
    for pkg in &auto_blocks {
        copy_glob_patterns(
            &pkg.assets.copy,
            &pkg.source_root,
            plugin_output_dir,
            pkg.assets.dest.as_deref(),
        )?;
    }
    for out in written_outputs {
        plugin.inject_post_compilation_assets(out, &auto_assets)?;
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

Then call it from the loop:

```rust
